  "docs": {
    "handle/claim.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.claim\n\nClaim a free name and make it the address of your public page, with its profile.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | handle.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`claim`: from nothing (it creates) to claimed, emitting HandleClaimed.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.claim.load` (database)\n- `handle.claim.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleTaken | 10 | HN-001 | declared in errors.ts |\n| HandleAlreadyOwned | 12 | HN-002 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle claim --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/claim` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.claim(payload)`.\n",
    "handle/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle\n\nA public name that belongs to one person until they release it, and is the address of a public page.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| name | HandleName |\n| owner | id |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: claimed, released. A move from the wrong state is refused HandleNotClaimed (exit 11).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| claim | (creates) | claimed | HandleClaimed |\n| release | claimed | released | HandleReleased |\n\n## Unique\n\n- name: unique while claimed\n- owner: unique while claimed\n\n## Roles\n\n- handleOwner\n\n## Operations\n\n- [handle.claim](claim.md): Claim a free name and make it the address of your public page, with its profile.\n- [handle.release](release.md): Free your name and take its public page offline. Anyone may claim the name afterwards.\n- [handle.resolve](resolve.md): Find the handle that holds a claimed name. A released or unclaimed name has none.\n",
    "handle/release.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.release\n\nFree your name and take its public page offline. Anyone may claim the name afterwards.\n\n**Who may call:** the handleOwner of the handle.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`release`: from claimed to released, emitting HandleReleased.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.release.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleNotClaimed | 11 | HN-900 | the handle is in a state release can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the handleOwner of the handle; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle release --handle <handle>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/release` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.release(payload)`.\n",
    "handle/resolve.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# handle.resolve\n\nFind the handle that holds a claimed name. A released or unclaimed name has none.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| name | handle.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.id |\n\n## Steps\n\n- `handle.resolve.load` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HandleNotFound | 13 | HN-003 | declared in errors.ts |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in handle resolve --name <name>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /handle/resolve` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.handle.resolve(payload)`.\n",
    "link/add.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.add\n\nAppend a link to your own public page. You need a claimed name first.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone signed in.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| title | link.title |\n| url | link.url |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`add`: from nothing (it creates) to listed, emitting LinkAdded.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.add.load` (database)\n- `link.add.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkNeedsHandle | 30 | LN-001 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't anyone signed in; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link add --title <title> --url <url>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/add` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.add(payload)`.\n",
    "link/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link\n\nA title and web address on a public page.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| profile | profile.id |\n| owner | handle.owner |\n| title | LinkTitle |\n| url | LinkUrl |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: listed, removed. A move from the wrong state is refused LinkNotListed (exit 31).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| add | (creates) | listed | LinkAdded |\n| remove | listed | removed | LinkRemoved |\n\n## Roles\n\n- linkOwner\n\n## Operations\n\n- [link.add](add.md): Append a link to your own public page. You need a claimed name first.\n- [link.order](order.md): Move a link to a zero-based position. A position past the end puts it last.\n- [link.remove](remove.md): Remove a link from a public page.\n",
    "link/order.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.order\n\nMove a link to a zero-based position. A position past the end puts it last.\n\n**Who may call:** the linkOwner of the link.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n| position | LinkPosition |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.order.load` (database)\n- `link.order.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkAlreadyRemoved | 32 | LN-002 | declared in errors.ts |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the linkOwner of the link; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link order --link <link> --position <position>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/order` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.order(payload)`.\n",
    "link/remove.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# link.remove\n\nRemove a link from a public page.\n\n**Who may call:** the linkOwner of the link.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| link | link.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`remove`: from listed to removed, emitting LinkRemoved.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `link.remove.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LinkNotListed | 31 | LN-900 | the link is in a state remove can't start from; carries `state` |\n| NotAllowed | 3 | AR-001 | the caller isn't the linkOwner of the link; the handler never runs |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in link remove --link <link>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /link/remove` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.link.remove(payload)`.\n",
    "profile/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# profile.get\n\nRead a claimed name's public page and its links in display order.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.name |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| handle | handle.name |\n| links | schema |\n\n## Steps\n\n- `profile.get.load` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ProfileNotFound | 20 | PR-001 | declared in errors.ts |\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nplugged-in profile get --handle <handle>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /profile/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.profile.get(payload)`.\n",
    "profile/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# profile\n\nA claimed name's public page, with its links in the order they were put.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| handle | handle.id |\n| links | schema |\n\n## Unique\n\n- handle: unique in every state\n\n## Operations\n\n- [profile.get](get.md): Read a claimed name's public page and its links in display order.\n"
  },
